                    <tr><td>Cabinet materials (custom)</td><td>$500 – $1,200+/linear ft</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>Labor / installation</td><td>$50 – $150/hour</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>Hardware</td><td>$3 – $50+ per piece</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>Soft-close upgrades</td><td>$25 – $75 per door/drawer</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>Customization features</td><td>$200 – $2,000+</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>Old cabinet removal</td><td>$300 – $700</td></tr>
                  </tbody>
                </table>
              </div>

              <h3>Materials</h3>
              <p>The material you choose is the biggest cost driver. Solid wood (maple, cherry, oak) commands premium pricing, while MDF and plywood offer durability at lower costs.</p>

              <h3>Labor</h3>
              <p>In Pennsylvania, professional cabinet installation typically runs $50–$150 per hour. Most kitchen installs take 1–3 days depending on complexity.</p>

              <h3>Installation</h3>
              <p>Installation costs include not just hanging the cabinets, but also leveling, shimming, scribing to walls, and toe-kick installation.</p>

              <h3>Hardware</h3>
              <p>Handles, knobs, hinges, and soft-close mechanisms add up quickly. A full kitchen with 30 doors and drawers can require $300–$1,500 in hardware alone.</p>

              <h3>Customization</h3>
              <p>Custom features like pull-out shelves, built-in spice racks, lazy Susans, glass-front doors, and integrated lighting can add $500–$5,000+ to your total cabinet budget.</p>
            </div>

