            <!-- Cabinet Styles -->
            <div class="post-body__section reveal">
              <h2>Popular Kitchen Cabinet Styles &amp; Price Impact</h2>

              <h3>Shaker Cabinets</h3>
              <p>Shaker cabinets remain the most popular style in Media, PA and nationally. Their clean, recessed-panel design works with traditional and contemporary kitchens alike. Shaker doors add $15–$50 per door over basic flat-panel pricing. For real-world cost benchmarks, the <a href="https://www.remodeling.hw.net/cost-vs-value/2025/" rel="noopener" target="_blank">Remodeling Magazine Cost vs. Value Report</a> tracks kitchen remodel ROI data annually across U.S. markets including the Philadelphia metro area.</p>

              <h3>Flat Panel (Modern)</h3>
              <p>Flat-panel or slab-door cabinets are popular in modern and minimalist kitchen designs. They're often less expensive to manufacture than shaker styles and are the default for European-style frameless cabinets.</p>

              <h3>Raised Panel</h3>
              <p>Raised panel doors have a traditional, formal look common in older Delaware County homes. They cost $20–$75 more per door than flat panels due to more complex milling.</p>

              <h3>Glass-Front Cabinets</h3>
              <p>Glass-front cabinets add visual interest and a high-end look to upper cabinet runs. Expect to add $50–$200+ per door for glass inserts, plus the cost of interior cabinet lighting if desired.</p>
