                <li><strong>Cabinet refacing:</strong> Replace just doors and drawer fronts; costs 40–60% less than full replacement.</li>
                <li><strong>Buy during sales:</strong> January and July sales can save 20–30%.</li>
                <li><strong>Choose semi-custom over custom:</strong> Get 80% quality at 50% price in most cases.</li>
                <li><strong>Mix materials strategically:</strong> Use solid wood/glass on upper cabinets; lower-cost materials on base cabinets.</li>
                <li><strong>Keep existing layout:</strong> Moving plumbing/electrical adds $1,000–$5,000+.</li>
                <li><strong>Order extra:</strong> Ordering extra doors during initial order costs far less than future reorders.</li>
              </ul>
            </div>

            <!-- Hidden Costs -->
            <div class="post-body__section reveal">
              <h2>Hidden Costs Most Homeowners Miss</h2>
              <p>A good rule of thumb: add 10-15% to your cabinet budget as a contingency for hidden costs.</p>
              <ul class="post-list">
                <li>Removal and disposal of old cabinets: $300 – $700</li>
                <li>Wall repairs (if required): $200 – $800</li>
                <li>Electrical adjustments: $150 – $600</li>
                <li>Plumbing adjustments: $300 – $1,500</li>
                <li>Countertop templating and replacement: $2,000 – $8,000+</li>
                <li>Permit fees: $75 – $300</li>
                <li>Touch-up paint: $50 – $200</li>
              </ul>
            </div>
            <div class="post-body__section reveal">
              <h2>Frequently Asked Questions About Kitchen Cabinet Costs</h2>
              <div class="post-faq">
                <div class="post-faq__item reveal">
                  <h3>How much do kitchen cabinets cost in Media, PA?</h3>
                  <p>Kitchen cabinet costs in <strong>Media, PA</strong> and the surrounding <strong>Delaware County</strong> area range from <strong>$3,000–$8,000</strong> for stock cabinets, <strong>$8,000–$20,000</strong> for semi-custom, and <strong>$20,000–$50,000+</strong> for fully custom cabinets. Per linear foot pricing runs <strong>$60–$200 for stock</strong>, <strong>$100–$650 for semi-custom</strong>, and <strong>$500–$1,200+</strong> for custom. Small kitchens typically land at the lower end; large open-concept kitchens can reach $30,000–$60,000 for premium options.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="post-faq__item reveal">
                  <h3>What is the cheapest type of kitchen cabinet?</h3>
                  <p><strong>Stock kitchen cabinets</strong> are the most affordable option, typically costing <strong>$60–$200 per linear foot</strong>, with a full kitchen installation running <strong>$3,000–$8,000 total</strong>. They are available immediately from major retailers and work well for budget remodels, rental properties, and flips where a quick turnaround matters more than a perfect fit. The trade-off: limited styles, standard sizes only, and lower material quality compared to semi-custom or custom options.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="post-faq__item reveal">
                  <h3>What hidden costs should I budget for when replacing kitchen cabinets?</h3>
                  <p>Add a <strong>10–15% contingency</strong> beyond your cabinet budget for hidden costs that commonly surface during installation: <strong>removal and disposal of old cabinets ($300–$700)</strong>, wall repairs if damage is found behind them <strong>($200–$800)</strong>, electrical adjustments <strong>($150–$600)</strong>, plumbing adjustments <strong>($300–$1,500)</strong>, countertop replacement <strong>($2,000–$8,000+)</strong>, and permit fees <strong>($75–$300)</strong>. These are not surprises with ProBrothers — we surface them in the initial assessment.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="post-faq__item reveal">
                  <h3>How long does it take to get custom kitchen cabinets made and installed?</h3>
                  <p>Timeline depends on the cabinet type. <strong>Stock cabinets</strong> are available within 1–2 weeks. <strong>Semi-custom cabinets</strong> have a manufacturing lead time of <strong>4–8 weeks</strong>. <strong>Fully custom cabinets</strong> take <strong>4–16 weeks</strong> from order to delivery. Add 1–3 days for professional installation (more for large or complex kitchens). ProBrothers factors lead times into your project schedule upfront so the kitchen remodel timeline is realistic from day one.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="post-faq__item reveal">
                  <h3>Are custom kitchen cabinets worth the extra cost?</h3>
                  <p>For a <strong>forever home</strong> or a kitchen you plan to use for 10+ years, custom cabinets are worth the premium. They offer a perfect fit for non-standard layouts (including corner solutions, around-window runs, and ceiling-height installations), premium material choice, unlimited design flexibility, and significantly higher resale value. In competitive <strong>Delaware County and Main Line PA</strong> markets, custom cabinetry is one of the first things buyers notice and value. The <a href="https://www.remodeling.hw.net/cost-vs-value/2025/" rel="noopener" target="_blank">Remodeling Magazine Cost vs. Value Report</a> consistently ranks kitchen upgrades among the top home improvement projects for resale return.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="post-faq__item reveal">
                  <h3>What is the difference between framed and frameless kitchen cabinets?</h3>
                  <p><strong>Framed (face-frame) cabinets</strong> have a solid wood frame on the front of the box, providing a more traditional look common in Colonial and craftsman-style <strong>Pennsylvania homes</strong>. They are slightly less storage-efficient due to the frame narrowing the opening. <strong>Frameless (European-style) cabinets</strong> have no front frame — doors mount directly to the box — giving a cleaner, more modern look and slightly more accessible storage. Both styles are available at custom, semi-custom, and stock levels.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="post-faq__item reveal">
                  <h3>Can I save money by doing cabinet refacing instead of full replacement?</h3>
                  <p>Yes — <strong>cabinet refacing</strong> replaces just the door fronts, drawer fronts, and visible exterior panels while keeping the existing cabinet boxes. It costs <strong>40–60% less than full replacement</strong> and can be completed in 2–4 days with minimal disruption. Refacing makes sense when: the box structure is still sound and square, you want to change the door style or color, and your kitchen layout already works well. ProBrothers offers both refacing and full replacement depending on your goals.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="post-faq__item reveal">
                  <h3>What cabinet materials hold up best in a high-use kitchen?</h3>
                  <p>For high-use kitchens in the <strong>Pennsylvania climate</strong>, the best-performing materials are: <strong>solid wood (maple, oak, cherry)</strong> for doors and face frames — extremely durable with proper finishing; <strong>plywood box construction</strong> rather than particleboard for the cabinet carcass — more moisture-resistant; and <strong>soft-close hardware</strong> on all hinges and drawer slides to reduce wear on the doors themselves. Avoid thermofoil on high-heat areas near ovens, as it can delaminate.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="post-faq__item reveal">
                  <h3>What is the most popular kitchen cabinet style in Delaware County, PA?</h3>
                  <p><strong>Shaker-style cabinets</strong> remain the top choice across <strong>Delaware County and Chester County</strong> in 2026. Their clean, recessed-panel design works with traditional Colonial homes, modern farmhouse aesthetics, and contemporary renovations alike. Shaker doors add only $15–$50 per door over basic flat-panel pricing, making them an excellent value. <strong>Flat-panel (slab) cabinets</strong> are popular in modern and minimalist kitchens; <strong>raised panel</strong> suits formal traditional spaces.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="post-faq__item reveal">
                  <h3>Does ProBrothers offer a free kitchen cabinet estimate?</h3>
                  <p>Yes. ProBrothers provides a <strong>free, no-obligation kitchen cabinet estimate</strong> for homeowners in <strong>Media, PA and Delaware County</strong>. The estimate covers custom design and installation, semi-custom and stock cabinet projects of all sizes, full kitchen remodeling, cabinet refacing, and custom carpentry or built-in storage. Contact the team at <strong>(484) 745-4097</strong> or via the website to schedule an in-home consultation.</p>
